WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.580
okay let's try a question
relating to spontaneity consider the

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:17.310
conversion of limestone to lime so we
have calcium carbonate caco3 yielding

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:25.920
calcium oxide CA o and co2 gas the
values of Delta H and Delta S are 179

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:32.550
point 1 kilojoules per mole and 160
point 2 joules per Kelvin respectively

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:38.489
at 298 K and 1 bar assuming that these
values do not change with temperature

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:44.850
what is the temperature above which
conversion of limestone to lime will be

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:51.030
spontaneous so we need to know some
things about Gibbs free energy enthalpy

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:55.620
entropy we need to know how those values
correlate we need to know something

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.570
about the conditions within which a
reaction will be spontaneous so go ahead

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:05.220
and check out my tutorial on Gibbs free
energy if you need some review and when

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.520
you're ready give it a try

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.260
so the first
thing we have to remember is that

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:30.150
reactions are spontaneous when Delta G
is less than zero so we need Delta G to

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:35.820
be negative in order for a reaction to
be spontaneous so if we have Delta G

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:41.520
equals Delta H minus T Delta s and we
need Delta G to be less than zero then

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.229
we also need Delta H minus T Delta s to
be less than zero because those are

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:51.869
equivalent now because we're trying to
figure out the temperature above which

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:55.829
conversion of limestone to lime will be
spontaneous that means we're going to be

00:01:55.829 --> 00:02:00.570
solving for a temperature so let's
rearrange this inequality to solve for

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:06.149
temperature all we do is add T Delta s
to both sides and then divide by Delta s

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:13.319
and we get T is greater than Delta H
over Delta S so we can just go ahead and

00:02:13.319 --> 00:02:16.920
plug in the
use that we know now we have 179.1

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:22.500
kilojoules per mole for Delta H but our
entropy value has joules so these are

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.580
gonna need to agree let's just go ahead
and multiply this one by a thousand that

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.670
way we'll have it in joules so one
hundred and seventy-nine thousand one

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:34.349
hundred joules per mole and then we can
divide that by a hundred and sixty point

00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:40.880
two joules per Kelvin that way the
joules will cancel and we end up with

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:48.060
1118 Kelvin so that means that despite
the enthalpic unfavorability we see that

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.930
this is endothermic right one hundred
seventy nine point one kilojoules per

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:56.640
mole this is an endothermic reaction
which we typically expect to not be

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.530
spontaneous however it is entropically
favorable we're producing more

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:05.610
substances we're producing a gas
therefore if we raise the temperature

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:10.829
high enough that T Delta s term will
outweigh the Delta H term and it happens

00:03:10.829 --> 00:03:18.740
to be this value 1118 Kelvin above that
temperature this will be a spontaneous process.

